 ],
 "notes": "One of Bonaire's few vertical walls: shore entry down the stairs at the yellow stone behind Dive Friends at Hamlet Oasis, a narrow reef plateau and, about 40-60 m out, a vertical wall from about 9 m to 22 m, then the reef slope to 40 m (divers-guide.com, bonaire.com, dive-centre pages). The steepest, narrowest stretch is just south of the stairs; sources disagree whether to swim north or south of the steel pipe marker. The steel pipe is placed just north of the stairs from a dive-centre description; the 30 m and 40 m contours and the route are illustrative. Coastline and dive-site markers © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). Positions are approximate.",
